'''''Echium simplex''''', commonly known as '''pride of Tenerife'''<ref name=GBIF/> or '''tower of jewels''', is an herbaceous [[biennial plant]] which grows up to {{cvt|3|m}} in height.

==Habitat==
It is a frost intolerant species requiring sustained periods of sunlight to thrive. It is endemic in the island of [[Tenerife]] mainly in [[Macizo de Anaga]].{{cn|date=March 2026}}

==Description==
The plant is biennial producing a dense rosette in the first year and producing the distinctive inflorescence to a height of {{convert|1|–|3|m}} during the second year. The [[flower]]s are white and the plant is in bloom from February to April in Tenerife. ''E. simplex'' is widely available as a garden flower in warm temperate areas. It is very attractive to [[bee]]s and produces a distinctively flavored [[honey]].{{cn|date=March 2026}}

